          necessary.  The -m switch is useful both  for  limiting
          address space consumption and guaranteeing access to an
          adequate amount of address space.

     -n _n_u_m_b_e_r
               Native-method zone  size.   If  set,  the  native-
          method  zone  size  will  be _n_u_m_b_e_r bytes.  The default
          native-method zone size varies from platform  to  plat-
          form,  ranging  from  approximately 400 KB to more than
          double that.

     -s _n_u_m_b_e_r
               Number of stacks.  If set, there  will  be  _n_u_m_b_e_r
          stacks.  By default there are 30.

     -v        Version     information.      Reports     detailed
          version/release    codes    meaningful   to   ParcPlace
          customer-support personnel.

     -w _n_u_m_b_e_r
               Sets the width of the Smalltalk  window  when  the
          system comes up (in pixels).  By default, the Smalltalk
          window will be the full size of the display.

